{
  "manufacturer": "ONICON",
  "manufacturer_slug": "onicon",
  "model": "System-1000 Flow and Energy Measurement System",
  "model_slug": "system-1000-btu-meter",
  "aliases": [
    "System-1000",
    "SYS-1000",
    "SYS-1100-111",
    "SYS-1100-121",
    "SYS-1200-111",
    "SYS-1200-121",
    "ONICON System 1000 BTU meter"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "BTU (energy) meter, two-channel",
  "applies_to": "ONICON System-1000 flow and energy (BTU) meters, single or two-channel, with the BACnet MS/TP or BACnet IP network option.",
  "summary": "The System-1000 is a one- or two-channel BTU meter with native BACnet MS/TP or BACnet IP. Per channel it exposes energy rate, flow, supply, return and delta temperature, an aux input and COP as Analog Inputs, and energy, volume and aux totals (non-resettable, year-to-date, previous year and resettable user totals) as Analog Values. Binary Inputs give mode, alarms and a system fault.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP",
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": "Firmware 1.x (PICS: firmware 1.3.0, application 1.26.1)",
  "default_device_instance": 57017,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "The object list prints 'AI 6' twice: once for Delta Temp Ch. 1 and once for AUX Input Ch. 1. Delta Temp Ch. 1 is listed here as AI 5, the gap in the sequence; confirm on the meter.",
    "The table gives no units. Defaults shown are typical US units; energy, flow and temperature units are set on the meter.",
    "Channel 2 objects (AI 8-15, AV 20-39, BI 2-3) carry data only on two-channel models. AI 16 (net rate between channels) is used only when configured.",
    "Access is not in the object list. The PICS says the 'user defined' and aux pulse totals can be reset by writing 0; the resettable User totals are marked W here, all else R.",
    "BI 2 is printed with the description 'current flow direction' and BI 3 with the mode text; the names suggest the descriptions are swapped by one row.",
    "BI 8 is not listed."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "System-1000 Flow and Energy Measurement System Installation and Operation Guide",
    "doc_number": "DOC-0008270 Rev.B",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.onicon.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/System-1000-manual-DOC-0008270.pdf"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Set the MS/TP address (default 128 is a slave address, so it must be changed to 0-127) or the IP settings from the meter menu, then power-cycle. Read energy rate, flow, temperatures and the energy totals for each channel, plus the alarm and fault BIs.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "AI 0",
        "name": "Energy Rate Ch. 1",
        "why": "Channel 1 thermal energy rate"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 1",
        "name": "Volume Rate Ch. 1",
        "why": "Channel 1 flow rate"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 3",
        "name": "Supply Temp Ch. 1",
        "why": "Channel 1 supply temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 4",
        "name": "Return Temp Ch. 1",
        "why": "Channel 1 return temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 0",
        "name": "Energy Total Mode 1 Ch. 1",
        "why": "Channel 1 energy total, non-resettable (mode 1)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 8",
        "name": "Volume Total Mode 1 Ch. 1",
        "why": "Channel 1 volume total, non-resettable (mode 1)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 0",
        "name": "Mode Indication Ch. 1",
        "why": "Channel 1 mode: cooling/forward or heating/reverse"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 1",
        "name": "Alarm Ch. 1",
        "why": "Channel 1 reading outside its limits"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 9",
        "name": "System Fault",
        "why": "Meter system error"
      }
    ],
    "enable": null,
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "Menu: User Configurations > Network > BACnet MS/TP or BACnet UDP/IP.",
      "MS/TP defaults: 38400 baud, address 128 (slave, set 0-127 to communicate), device instance 57017, Max Master 127.",
      "BACnet IP defaults: IP 192.168.1.24, mask 255.255.255.0, UDP port 47808, instance 57017.",
      "Power-cycle the meter after any network change."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "The default MS/TP address 128 is a slave address; the meter will not join the token ring until it is set to 0-127.",
      "Two objects are printed as AI 6; check which instance holds Delta Temp Ch. 1.",
      "Only the User totals reset (write 0); the other totals are non-resettable."
    ]
  },
